 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry` now compiles static tool `inputSchema` definitions at `register` time, caches
+  compiled validators per schema object for function-valued definitions, and validates `input` in
+  `ToolRegistry.execute` before invoking the executor. Invalid schemas fail fast at registration
+  naming the tool, and rejected calls return a `ToolResponse` describing the failing property paths
+  and constraints — never property values — so the model can correct its call within `maxToolRounds`
+  instead of aborting the turn. **Migration:** executors that previously received malformed input to
+  build custom error messages now receive only input that satisfies `required`, declared types and
+  `enum` (undeclared extra properties still pass through unchanged).
+
